Package: dipsim
Type: Package
Title: Interactive Ashenfelter-Dip Simulator for the budgetsc Pipeline
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Andre", "Bonfrer", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "andre.bonfrer@deakin.edu.au")
Description: A standalone Shiny app that simulates panels in which adoption of a
    budgeting feature is triggered by a transitory shock (an Ashenfelter dip),
    runs the budgetsc synthetic-control stage on them, and shows how the bias
    depends on baseline length, held-out matching weeks, the number of matched
    outcomes, donor pool size and shock persistence. Built as a starting point
    for adding further remedies.
